@@ -0,0 +1,112 @@
+# OpenChatLink live conversation sync
+
+OpenChatLink's unpacked Chrome extension sends personal ChatGPT history directly
+to Phase Pal while the application is running. No hstry database, Python import
+process, or manual directory selection is needed for this flow.
+
+## User flow
+
+1. Load the OpenChatLink `phasepal-extension` folder in Chrome with Developer mode.
+2. Select the destination avatar in Phase Pal. Enable Store Chat History.
+3. In Chat Settings > General > External Conversations, enable personal ChatGPT
+   sync and copy the connection code into the extension.
+4. Click the extension icon to open its settings tab. Load the chat titles and
+   select specific conversations, or explicitly choose all personal chats.
+5. Choose all history, the last 100 visible messages per chat, or messages on or
+   after a chosen date (00:00 UTC). Choose automatic or manual sync, then save.
+   Automatic sync checks once per minute. Manual mode runs only when requested;
+   continuation batches finish that request without enabling recurring sync.
+6. Chats appear in Chat History as Chrome collects the chosen text. Initial
+   collection is limited to selected chats; no selection means no import.
+7. Sending text in a synced original first creates a local copy and submits
+   through the existing ChatV2 submit coordinator. The banner explains that
+   local changes cannot sync back and offers Open in ChatGPT or View synced
+   original. Continue in Phase Pal can also create the copy before voice or edits.
+
+The original remains a browser-owned snapshot. Local copies retain their
+history independently. Imported originals reject text/voice/MCP/reload submits
+that bypass copy preparation. Core history append, update, reaction, delete
+message, and truncation paths enforce the same write policy. Whole-chat deletion,
+pinning, and title renaming remain available. Deleted mirrors are not recreated.
+Any unexpected local modification causes a conflict instead of overwrite.
+
+Selecting chats is account-scoped. The picker fetches one page of titles at a
+time and does not fetch transcript bodies. Sync fetches bodies only for the
+chosen chats. Saved filters reset collection checkpoints when the chosen chats
+or history window change. A schedule change alone keeps the checkpoint.
+History limits apply before the text DTO is sent to the existing app receiver.
+Nonempty snapshots can update a mirror to a smaller window; local copies stay
+independent. Deselection stops future updates and leaves existing history in
+place. Chats with no matching text are skipped rather than deleted.
+
+Incoming chats belong to the avatar selected when sync was enabled. To change
+that destination, disable sync, select another avatar, then reconnect the
+extension. Existing chats and copies keep their owners. The explicit scoped
+runtime data path separates accounts, Steam channels, and Direct data.
+
+## Ownership and lifecycle
+
+ChatV2RuntimeCompositionService creates the host-scoped
+ChatV2ExternalConversationService against its existing raw history store.
+ChatV2RuntimeHostController starts/resumes it on enable, suspends it on disable,
+and disposes it on destruction. It is not a scene singleton or a Gateway sidecar.
+This follows the existing ChatV2 host composition boundary: the history store is
+host-scoped and must not be captured by an application-wide service.
+
+Imports, registry persistence, local-copy creation, socket work, and secure
+credential operations run asynchronously outside the frame path. A single
+history writer serializes imported snapshots and local copies. Frame polling
+drains completed IDs and refreshes visible source chats only when no attachments
+are pending. An unchanged browser replay does not reload the transcript.
+Copy completion is rejected after a session, character, or host lifetime change.
+The original composer draft is retained when preparation fails.
+
+The source registry is in Settings/external_conversations.json; preferences
+are in Settings/external_conversation_settings.json. Neither contains pairing
+credentials. The existing OS credential-store adapter accepts a scoped target
+name while preserving its original External Memory defaults.
+
+## Receiver contract
+
+- TCP/HTTP binds IPv4 127.0.0.1:41771 only. A second owner cannot take the port.
+- GET /openchatlink/v1/health and POST /openchatlink/v1/ingest require the copied
+  256-bit bearer credential. The protocol marker is `openchatlink/1`.
+- The expected Host is the exact loopback host/port. Website Origins are
+  rejected. Chrome-extension Origins receive bounded CORS/preflight responses.
+- Four clients, 16 KiB headers, 8 MiB bodies, depth 32, and 60-second request
+  cancellation bound receiver work. Transfer-Encoding is rejected.
+- No caller-supplied directory, avatar ID, URL, shell command, tool call, system
+  prompt, or executable configuration is accepted.
+- The text DTO contains one ChatGPT UUID, account scope, title, timestamp, and
+  ordered user/assistant messages. System and tool roles are rejected.
+- Source identity combines the ChatGPT account, conversation, and destination
+  avatar. Replays are idempotent; local copies use independent IDs.
+
+Only text is mirrored. ChatGPT browser credentials, attachments, saved memory,
+custom GPT instructions, and model state are not imported. This is not a
+ChatGPT conversation-write API. New replies use Phase Pal's selected provider
+and its existing tool approval and cancellation policy.
+
+## Verification
+
+The following managed checks were completed for the initial app integration.
+
+Four affected assemblies (Core, Runtime, Toolkit, Platform) compiled using their
+generated project source/reference lists and available Unity reference assemblies.
+No Unity process was launched.
+
+Seventeen behavior cases ran in a standalone managed harness against the production
+history store and receiver: import/replay, Unicode/timestamps, local copy/source
+independence, local conflict preservation, deleted mirrors after restart, Core
+write policy, role rejection, cancellation, HTTP ingestion/authentication/origin
+checks, secure pairing, consent revocation, late completions, and rejection before
+provider dispatch. Both character and global history stores were checked.
+Twenty-one Node tests now cover extension protocol, selected-chat and visible-text
+filtering, history limits, filter/checkpoint ownership, manual/automatic scheduling,
+restart continuation, cancellation, and revocation. A Chrome UI check with
+synthetic chat data verified picking chats across pages, selecting history/date
+limits, saving manual mode, and invoking Sync now. It did not access ChatGPT.
+
+Live Chrome extension loading, Phase Pal UI rendering, scene transitions, and packaged player QA
+still require a Phase Pal build containing this integration. The unchanged
+offline importer remains available as a separate fallback.
